WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.000
Step four reads the records.

2
00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:08.094
M C nine hundred thousand and one is
a retirement, of Basic authentication

3
00:00:08.094 --> 00:00:13.488
for S M T P AUTH client submission,
due on January thirty-first, 2027.

4
00:00:13.488 --> 00:00:16.338
M C nine hundred thousand
and three is a change,

5
00:00:16.338 --> 00:00:21.138
an update to SharePoint Framework solutions,
and it needs action with no date.

6
00:00:21.138 --> 00:00:25.187
The incident is open, and the
resolved Teams issue is closed.

7
00:00:25.187 --> 00:00:28.326
Step five asks who said
each one needs action.

8
00:00:28.326 --> 00:00:30.818
For the retirement, it was Microsoft:

9
00:00:30.818 --> 00:00:33.975
the basis is provider,
action-required-by date.

10
00:00:33.975 --> 00:00:38.517
For the SharePoint change, it was the
kit's rule: a prevent-or-fix-issue post

11
00:00:38.517 --> 00:00:43.287
without a date is action required, and
the record says rule, with the category.

12
00:00:43.287 --> 00:00:44.913
Everything else says none.

13
00:00:44.913 --> 00:00:48.745
So when someone asks where a date
came from, the record answers,

14
00:00:48.745 --> 00:00:51.960
and where Microsoft gave
none, the kit makes none up.
